- op: discuss  # aecf
  at: '2026-11-17T13:15:50Z'  # aecf
  by: agent  # aecf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aecf
  clock: 8  # aecf
  nonce: aecf  # aecf
  message: "Merged in PR #2226 (dev: commit 'feat(smart-test): select from a stored graph; analyse only when it may not answer'). CLOSE CONDITION, RUN: (1) LIVE in the main checkout, on the branch's change to package source (graph_rows.py, graph_select.py, selection_log.py): `smart-test --manifest` with no usable stored graph 345 s (it analysed and stored graph 1); the next `smart-test --manifest` 14 s, printing '[smart-test] selecting from stored graph 1 of fd5448d16, 0 commit(s) old: 11 seed file(s), 0 of them not this change's, reaching 0 test file(s) this change does not; 205 file(s) named'; 404 selected test files against the analysed run's 393, none of the 393 missing (the 11 more: every changed file is seeded, not package source only). switch/live.txt. The PR's own committed manifest was selected that way; its header: '# Graph: stored graph 1 of fd5448d16, 2 commit(s) old: 13 seed file(s), 0 of them not this change's, ...'. (2) EACH FALLBACK HAS A TEST AND A MUTATION: no usable graph (exit 3: none stored, another build, too old, a tree git does not have), failed (4), an added file (5), too far behind (6), an unreadable analyzer build, --fresh-graph, CI / nested / target mode; 34 text mutations, 33 red, the survivor a condition another implied, removed (switch/mutations.tsv). (3) Documented: .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/smart-test-playbook.md, section 'Where the selection comes from: a stored graph'. WHAT DIFFERS FROM THE DESCRIPTION: seeds are the change's files PLUS every file that differs from the graph's tree (see the note of 11-17 above); the comparison that stays on is now 'what graph-select would have answered' against the fresh answer, in stale-record; the survey registry is removed. MY CHOICE, NOT A RULING, FOR THE OWNER TO CONFIRM OR CHANGE: a stored graph is refused when its age adds more than 150 test files that are not the change's (MAX_EXTRA_TESTS in scripts/coverage-select). NOT SHOWN: a refused graph in a LIVE run other than 'no usable stored graph' (the other refusals are shown by tests on small repositories); a STORED GRAPH LOST line has not occurred. KNOWN GAPS, EACH ITS OWN ITEM: nothing renews a graph except a refusal (WI-tupup-garak); worktree runs still analyse (WI-kitin-rirup)."  # aecf
